{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And every armed man shall cross over before you.</b> It was not enough for him what he said, ״if you arm yourselves״ — he came to stipulate something that was not mentioned in their words, namely, that all of them shall cross over — meaning, every one fit for armed service. Yet it is still difficult: he should have said in the first verse ״if you all arm yourselves״ or ״if you all cross over armed.״" "<b>However,</b> the intent of Moses in this is a promise and a declaration of the precise implication heard along this line — that <b>if you do</b> etc. <b>and you arm yourselves</b> etc., he promises that not one of them will fall, and they will be whole and numerous. And that is his saying <b>and every armed man shall cross over</b> — meaning, all of them, and not one will be missing from them. And from this implication you hear that if they do not do what was said, they are destined for destruction. And according to this interpretation, the statement <b>and…shall cross over</b> etc. is an inference regarding the preceding verse, which was not a condition dependent on action — for the condition he had already stated: ״if you do this thing,״ whose meaning is the condition that they themselves stipulated, as I wrote above. And his saying <b>before YHWH</b> is to say that in this there will be no screen separating between them and YHWH, as it says (Isaiah 59:2) ״your iniquities have been separating between you and your Elohim״ — that the designations of the wicked and their hosts are the separators, and they are the corrupters." "<b>Further,</b> it is intended to say <b>before YHWH</b> — meaning, that it is He who dispossesses His enemies, as Scripture concludes, ״until He dispossesses״ — meaning, YHWH — ״His enemies from before Him.״ And according to this interpretation, the measurement of the verse is along this line: <b>if you arm yourselves</b> and your intent will be before YHWH etc., then you do not need battle but merely to cross over before YHWH, and He will dispossess His enemies. And that is his saying ״and…you shall cross over…before YHWH,״ who goes forth to take vengeance, until He dispossesses His enemies. From this you have learned that it is He who dispossesses before the children of Israel. And he was precise in saying <b>from before Him</b>, because YHWH dwells in the city He chose for Himself, the beloved Jerusalem, and He does not wish to see His enemies before Him."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:51.453421771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}